      "cooked": "<p>Context: I have created a Multi-Level BOM. Each layer of BOM has their own operations and respectively their sequence of operations.</p>\n<p>Coincidentally the finish product BOM and the subassembly BOM may have the same operations within them</p>\n<p>Problem: When I tick “Use Multi-Level BOM” to create the Work Order. The sequence of BOM gets confused and the Sub Assembly’s sequence of operation all turn into 0, this leads to an error.</p>\n<p>I can circumvent the error by manually adjusting the sequence of operations in the Work Order.</p>\n<p>I would like a second opinion if I really have to manually edit it or did I configure something wrong?</p>\n<p>Thank you</p>\n<p><div class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"><a class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/original/3X/5/8/58b61ff8cca424f2a76a6fba6fc3699772ca9d63.jpeg\" data-download-href=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/58b61ff8cca424f2a76a6fba6fc3699772ca9d63\" title=\"image\"><img src=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/optimized/3X/5/8/58b61ff8cca424f2a76a6fba6fc3699772ca9d63_2_690x251.jpeg\" alt=\"image\" data-base62-sha1=\"cEMdwFH4bHYF1gM8sI3LlJsq4Kv\" width=\"690\" height=\"251\" srcset=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/optimized/3X/5/8/58b61ff8cca424f2a76a6fba6fc3699772ca9d63_2_690x251.jpeg, https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/optimized/3X/5/8/58b61ff8cca424f2a76a6fba6fc3699772ca9d63_2_1035x376.jpeg 1.5x, https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/original/3X/5/8/58b61ff8cca424f2a76a6fba6fc3699772ca9d63.jpeg 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"FAFAFA\"><div class=\"meta\"><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#far-image\"></use></svg><span class=\"filename\">image</span><span class=\"informations\">1280×467 60.3 KB</span><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#discourse-expand\"></use></svg></div></a></div></p>",
